A||||4||loafer87gt||Getting engine rebuilt, what performance parts to get?||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||03-06-2001||01:41 PM||||Man this week is turning out great! My friend just called and he needs a project car and an engine to rebuild before he can complete his mechanical course. He has been building smallblocks chevs since I've known him, so I'm confident in his work. The technical school pays for all the labour and machine work, I just have to pay for the parts, which the school can get for 5% over cost. What sort of performance parts should I tell him order to get a bit more performance and reliabity out of the my old 87 v6? I was thinking about SI valves, and a crane compucam. Also, what is the final verdict of roller rockers? If I went for the factory 1.5 ratio would it improve efficiency without causing extra wear on my valve guides? Also, is there any pistons a guy can get that raise the compression ratio? I can't really afford forged pistons, but is there a hyperteutic replacement that gives around 9:1 compression? I think I read in the forum that the 3.4 DOHC pistons would work, but do any other modifications need to be done to use them? I am super excited, I have been without my Fiero for about a year now, and he said he should be able to have it on the road by the end of the month.||||reg||1
Z||000001||loafer87gt||03-06-2001||03:42 PM||||Also, don't want to start a flame war here, but being as my EGR tube is severely cracked, would it damage my engine to bypass the EGR? All the stories I have heard about toasted pistons are always second hand, has anyone who bypassed there EGR run into problems? What would be the best way to go about bypassing it? Blocking it or simply disconnecting it?||||reg||1
Z||000002||ironhedno3||03-06-2001||06:29 PM||||keep the egr..either fix the tube or get another..its there for a reason..as far as going over 9:1 compression..dont do it unless you have installed a knock sensor or are using race gas...surely you dont wanna detonate your new engine||||reg||6
